  "source": "EAMCET 2009 (Medical)",
  "question": "The volume of mercury in the bulb of a thermometer is $10^{-6}\\ \\text{m}^3$. The area of cross-section of the capillary tube is $2 \\times 10^{-7}\\ \\text{m}^2$. If the temperature is raised by $100°$C, the increase in the length of the mercury column is ($\\gamma_{Hg} = 18 \\times 10^{-5}\\ °\\text{C}^{-1}$)",
  "diagram": "",
  "diagram_alt": "",
  "options": [
